// A shell, in Omega. This is the word split bash does before it runs anything:
// unquoted space, tab and newline separate words; single quotes are literal;
// double quotes keep spaces; a backslash outside quotes keeps the next byte;
// an unquoted # starts a comment; an unquoted | separates commands and is not
// a word. An unclosed quote refuses. The exec itself is not here yet.
